From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:21:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] scl: carry placement across the buffer command's
 network dup

Abc_SclBufferingPerform returns a fresh Abc_NtkDupDfs of the buffered
network; like topo, that dup drops node names, so a loaded placement
went stale. Scl_PlaceTransfer now rides the pCopy pointers; new
buffers stay uncoordinated and fall back to the wire-load table in
subsequent sizing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/map/scl/scl.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/map/scl/scl.c b/src/map/scl/scl.c
index a43529972..b108933fb 100644
--- a/src/map/scl/scl.c
+++ b/src/map/scl/scl.c
@@ -1266,6 +1266,11 @@ int Scl_CommandBuffer( Abc_Frame_t * pAbc, int argc, char ** argv )
     }
     // modify the current network
     pNtkRes = Abc_SclBufferingPerform( pNtk, (SC_Lib *)pAbc->pLibScl, pPars );
+    // carry a loaded placement across the internal DupDfs (node names do
+    // not survive it); new buffers stay uncoordinated and fall back to the
+    // wire-load table in later sizing
+    if ( pNtkRes != NULL )
+        Scl_PlaceTransfer( pNtk, pNtkRes );
     if ( pNtkRes == NULL )
     {
         Abc_Print( -1, "The command has failed.\n" );
-- 
